WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.432
Welcome to Bible and Beyond.

2
00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:05.883
A free place to read, search, and study the Bible.

3
00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:11.105
Bible and Beyond is free, non-commercial, and has no ads.

4
00:00:11.105 --> 00:00:20.049
The welcome page shows everything in one place: Bibles, classic commentaries, daily devotionals, other Christian books, and music.

5
00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:23.214
Each part has buttons to read it or search it.

6
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.952
Let's start with the Bible reader.

7
00:00:28.952 --> 00:00:35.365
Choose a Bible, a book, and a chapter, then just keep scrolling to read on from chapter to chapter.

8
00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:37.437
Here we jump to John, chapter 3.

9
00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:45.405
Click any verse number for more: see it in context, in other translations, related verses, commentaries, or your own notes.

10
00:00:45.405 --> 00:00:54.667
In the Berean Standard Bible, you can click any word to see the original Hebrew or Greek word behind it, and every other verse where it's used.

11
00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:17.611
Search the Bible by words, an exact phrase, or a Strong's number, in one Bible or several.

12
00:01:17.611 --> 00:01:20.158
Here we search for, love one another.

13
00:01:20.158 --> 00:01:22.016
Every result links to more.

14
00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:26.008
Related Verses shows cross references, best matches first.

15
00:01:26.008 --> 00:01:30.895
And Other Translations shows the same verse in every Bible on the site.

16
00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:55.368
Search Everything looks through the Bible, the commentaries, the devotionals, the other books, and the music, all at once.

17
00:01:55.368 --> 00:02:00.902
Here, a search for grace finds the verses first, then what the commentators wrote about it.

18
00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:16.427
The commentaries include classic works by Matthew Henry, John Gill, John Calvin, Spurgeon, Luther, and more.

19
00:02:16.427 --> 00:02:21.482
Pick a commentary, a book, and a chapter, and read it chapter by chapter.

20
00:02:21.482 --> 00:02:24.874
Every Scripture reference is a link to the verse.

21
00:02:33.416 --> 00:02:40.935
You can also search the commentaries, to find what the great teachers wrote about any word or phrase, like, born again.

22
00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.751
Devotionals open at today's date.

23
00:02:48.751 --> 00:02:54.342
Here is Spurgeon's Morning and Evening, with a reading for every morning and evening of the year.

24
00:03:01.616 --> 00:03:09.867
Other books include Augustine, Aquinas, Chesterton, Bunyan, Tozer, and more, read a chapter at a time.

25
00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:16.182
In the Apostles' Creed, every statement links to the Bible verse it comes from.

26
00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.823
Christian music has hymns and songs to listen to, with their words shown alongside.

27
00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:42.423
And you can search the music by title, author, or the words of the song.

28
00:03:50.216 --> 00:03:54.461
The FAQ answers 32 common questions about the Bible and the faith.

29
00:03:54.461 --> 00:04:00.057
The answers are written by Google's Gemini AI, with every Scripture reference a link.

30
00:04:00.057 --> 00:04:00.572
The AI

31
00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:03.145
can make mistakes, and the page says so.

32
00:04:08.016 --> 00:04:10.588
With a free account, you can do even more.

33
00:04:11.888 --> 00:04:14.362
Everything works without an account.

34
00:04:14.362 --> 00:04:20.547
But a free account adds your own notes, daily devotional emails, and, on request, the AI

35
00:04:20.547 --> 00:04:21.165
features.

36
00:04:21.165 --> 00:04:23.639
Setting one up takes about a minute.

37
00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:26.937
All you need is an email address and a password.

38
00:04:26.937 --> 00:04:28.106
Then just log in.

39
00:04:42.688 --> 00:04:43.215
With AI

40
00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:49.244
search, you describe what you're looking for in your own words, such as, comfort when someone has died.

41
00:04:56.688 --> 00:04:57.199
The AI

42
00:04:57.199 --> 00:05:03.393
suggests verses from the Bibles on the site, each with the same links as any other search result.

43
00:05:08.888 --> 00:05:11.146
You can also ask your own question.

44
00:05:11.146 --> 00:05:14.306
Here we ask, what does the Bible say about worry?

45
00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:26.494
The answer comes back with every Scripture reference as a link.

46
00:05:35.488 --> 00:05:38.411
Any devotional can be emailed to you each day.

47
00:05:38.411 --> 00:05:42.033
Choose the time and your time zone, and press the button.

48
00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:45.846
Now Morning and Evening arrives at six thirty every morning.

49
00:05:45.846 --> 00:05:49.531
You can change the time, or stop the emails, at any point.

50
00:06:01.888 --> 00:06:07.174
You can write your own notes on any verse, commentary note, or devotional reading.

51
00:06:07.174 --> 00:06:11.300
Click a verse number, choose Notes, type your note, and save it.

52
00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:16.780
My Notes keeps every note in one place, with a search, and a link back to each verse.

53
00:06:50.222 --> 00:06:55.234
And if you need it, the Help page is a full user guide, with pictures of every feature.

54
00:06:59.855 --> 00:07:03.986
Try Bible and Beyond today, at bible-and-beyond.com.

55
00:07:03.986 --> 00:07:07.453
It's free, with no ads, and nothing to install.
